        "original_id": "dfef5115-721a-5e52-90ac-8cee5c193035",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: Miami Dolphins, Kansas City Chiefs, New York Jets, Denver Broncos\n- People: Andy Reid, John Dorsey\n- Seasons: 2016 Miami Dolphins season, 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season\n- Roles: head coach, general manager\n- Events: Week 15 win, playoff berth, John Dorsey firing\n\nFacts:\n- The 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season was the franchise's 47th season in the National Football League and its 57th overall season.\n- The 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season was Andy Reid's fourth season as head coach.\n- The 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season was John Dorsey's fourth and final season as general manager.\n- In Week 15 of the 2016 season, the Miami Dolphins defeated the New York Jets and clinched a winning record for the first time since 2008.\n- The following week, the Miami Dolphins clinched a playoff berth after the Kansas City Chiefs defeated the Denver Broncos.\n- John Dorsey was fired on June 22, 2017.",
